id: pm-jev-2mg8
title: Calibrate triage type proposals for projects with many item types
description: "Measured 2026-10-14 on a copy of the pm-jev tracker with the local tev1:4b model: triage proposed type Decision at p=0.30 for an item that is an Issue. The apply threshold of 0.8 kept it from being written, so it did no harm, but the proposal is wrong and wastes reviewer attention. Projects with many registered types (built-in plus custom types such as Decision, Knowledge, Run or Generation) dilute the label set, and the prompt does not tell the model what each type means. Triage should present each candidate type with its definition, prefer keeping the current type unless the evidence is strong, abstain when the top two labels are close, and report a measured per-type precision against a labelled dataset."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: calibration,decisions,triage
created_at: "2026-10-14T19:42:55.763Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-14T21:59:54.910Z"
author: claude-hub
acceptance_criteria: Triage presents every candidate type with a one-line definition drawn from the project's type registry; a keep-current-type option exists and is chosen when evidence is weak; triage abstains with an explicit reason when the margin between the top two labels is below a documented threshold; a labelled dataset that covers at least eight types including custom ones reports per-type precision and abstention rate with the real tev1 model; no type change below the apply threshold is ever written
comments[14]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-14T19:48:02.474Z",codex-agent,"Claimed and inspected the existing triage catalog, source guards, compact output, calibration harness and pinned SDK registry. Plan: explicit keep-current candidate bound per item, registry descriptions with folder metadata fallback, probability floor independent of apply flags, measured top-two margin abstention, and a balanced eight-type synthetic scratch-tracker comparison with held-out evaluation. No custom project labels will be hardcoded into production routing."
  "2026-10-14T19:56:39.864Z",codex-agent,"Implemented registry definitions, one-line custom folder fallback, item-bound keep-current candidate, code-owned probability ranking and explicit nullable type abstention. Independently restored the former no-abstention behavior: focused margin regression exited 1; independently restored the former no-keep behavior: focused keep-current regression exited 1. Restored source byte-for-byte and the two focused regressions pass. The real tev1 comparison is still running; no empirical cutoff has been installed yet."
  "2026-10-14T20:09:26.331Z",codex-agent,"Real local tev1:4b comparison complete: 48 labelled items, eight types, two SDK-registered custom types, thirteen actual type candidates; 96 validated calls with unchanged model digest. Frozen positive margin 0.05136322250317049 is fitted only on 24 calibration cases (23/24 correct). Held-out old prompt: 23/24 correct, 95.8% precision; new raw prompt: 24/24 correct, 100%; conservative policy: 23/24 correct, 95.8%, with 0/24 margin abstentions. The policy retains one initially misrouted Task below the 0.8 evidence floor; this trade-off is explicit in the report and per-type table. Report replay and 24 focused tests pass. The earlier noul report is unchanged."
  "2026-10-14T20:12:57.444Z",codex-agent,"Final coverage verification passes 141/141 tests and 100% statements, branches, functions and lines across all 12 inventoried authored TypeScript sources; duplication is 0%. Real tev1 test:live passes 2/2 tests, including single-item triage/dedupe/ask/safety gates and six batch requests with zero-request receipt reuse. The first linked release attempts caught duplicate test transport setup, now removed with a shared fixture helper; both full release gates are being rerun. pm test reports evidence tracking disabled by project policy, so results are retained in these comments rather than changing that policy."
  "2026-10-14T20:16:43.790Z",codex-agent,"Verified final gates with disposable HOME and Git identity config disabled: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each pass 141/141 tests with unchanged 100% statements/branches/functions/lines over all 12 source files, zero duplication, zero production audit findings and valid publication attestation. Real npm run test:live passes 2/2; changelog check and focused policy regressions pass. Additional safety proof: removing only the type apply-probability comparison makes the real-tracker regression fail (exit 1); restoring source byte-for-byte passes 1/1. Required commands were executed through the linked pm runner; automatic result recording is disabled by existing policy, so this comment records the sanitized receipt. Remaining limitation: one small synthetic run, zero measured held-out abstentions, and one misrouted Task conservatively retained below 0.8. Ready for PR delivery; leave the item in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-14T20:19:24.897Z",codex-agent,"Final review found a valid custom type named constructor inherited Object.prototype through the built-in fallback dictionary. Changed canonical lookup to a ReadonlyMap so every undescribed custom type uses its real folder metadata. A real temp-tracker regression passes; reverting only the safe definition lookup fails that regression (exit 1), and source was restored byte-for-byte. Reclaimed for this narrow final correction and rerunning all linked gates. Dataset prompts, model observations and frozen threshold are unchanged."
  "2026-10-14T20:24:49.755Z",codex-agent,"Final correction verified: all five linked commands pass with disposable HOME and Git identity config disabled. npm and Bun release gates each pass 141/141 tests and 100% of all four coverage dimensions across 12 sources; live acceptance passes 2/2 against tev1:4b; changelog check and both focused policy tests pass. Strict tracker health passes with disposable HOME and verifies storage integrity/history. Normal-environment health flags an unrelated extension/host compatibility mismatch; no pins, extension configuration or telemetry settings were changed. Definition lookup, keep-current, margin and apply-threshold revert proofs each fail independently and pass after byte-for-byte restoration. Ready for the requested feature PR; retain in_progress status for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-14T20:47:44.900Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1: verify effective type definitions against receipt reuse; add a stable question and policy fingerprint, append-only legacy invalidation, real-tracker regression coverage, and behavioural revert proof. Rebuild committed dist and run npm/Bun release gates before delivery."
  "2026-10-14T20:49:13.189Z",codex-agent,"Verified receipt reuse only checks catalog and source. Design: SHA-256 of the ordered effective type choice question with a stable keep-current placeholder, TYPE_MARGIN_THRESHOLD and TYPE_CHANGE_PROBABILITY. Placeholder binding includes the actual keep-current instruction template while preserving reuse after an applied routing change. Missing fingerprints are stale; all historical comments remain untouched."
  "2026-10-14T20:52:26.325Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: reverted only hasTriageReceipt to catalog/source matching, retaining fingerprint creation and all other code. node --test --test-reporter=spec --test-name-pattern=\"edited custom description|added type\" test/triage-receipt.test.ts ran 2 tests: 0 passed, 2 failed because each made 1 model call rather than the expected 2. Restored index.ts byte-for-byte. Fixed focused suite: 25/25 passed. Linked fingerprint command: 5/5 passed; PM automatic result tracking is disabled, so this sanitized comment records the evidence. Unchanged and normalized definitions, legacy migration and append-only history are covered."
  "2026-10-14T20:59:57.093Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1 verified: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each pass 146/146 tests, no skips, 100% statements/branches/functions/lines across all 12 authored sources, 0% duplication, no production vulnerabilities, and valid publication attestation. Both use disposable HOME with global/system Git configuration disabled; pack dry-run shasums match. Fingerprint inputs: JSON type choice question (kind, instructions, ordered candidate labels and normalized description/built-in/folder-fallback definitions), stable __keep_current__ binding template, margin_threshold=0.05136322250317049, type_change_probability=0.8. Five real-tracker fingerprint cases pass; historical comments remain identical and repeated unchanged runs make no requests. Focused triage suite passes 25/25; linked fingerprint runner passes 5/5. Strict tracker health passes with integrity/history_drift checks; existing advisory warnings remain outside this correction. Initial duplicate test fixture lines were consolidated without changing thresholds. Legacy receipt migration documented; dist rebuilt. No new blockers or SDK defects; linked result tracking remains disabled by existing policy and evidence is recorded here. Release claim for orchestrator verification; retain in_progress status."
  "2026-10-14T21:51:18.034Z",codex-agent,"Round 2: merged origin/main cleanly and verified all four findings. Plan: receipt stores expected post-run type and full-precision apply threshold; matching receipts skip equal or raised thresholds but revisit lower ones. Probability will measure the resolved type, with the keep-current candidate kept distinct. Legacy test will use the production unbounded projection and isolate missing fingerprint. Add real-tracker regressions and independent receipt-reuse revert proofs, then npm/Bun exact-coverage gates and regenerated artifacts."
  "2026-10-14T21:54:05.196Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proofs for findings 1 and 3: independently restored only hasTriageReceipt from reviewed head 0d2030f. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"external type change\" test/triage-receipt.test.ts failed 0/1 (external edit skipped instead of applied); node --test --test-name-pattern=\"lowered full-precision threshold\" test/triage-receipt.test.ts failed 0/1 (lower threshold skipped instead of applied). Restored index.ts byte-for-byte and combined focused run passed 2/2. Full receipt/type/batch focused suite passed 26/26. Tests import TypeScript directly, so revert runs did not require dist rebuild."
  "2026-10-14T21:59:53.362Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 complete: all four findings fixed; none refused. Receipts validate expected post-run type and full-precision apply threshold; equal or raised thresholds reuse, lower thresholds revisit. Resolved type probability is consistent across full/compact output, receipts and batch rows; docs distinguish historical semantics and unchanged raw calibration reports. Legacy fingerprint test uses production projection, asserts matching full-read source hash and seeds matching type/threshold metadata. npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 150/150, zero skips, 100% statements/branches/functions/lines across all 12 authored sources, 0% duplication, zero production audit findings and valid publication attestation. Both gates and the focused 26/26 suite passed through the pinned pm runner with disposable HOME and global/system Git configuration disabled. Independent finding 1 and 3 revert proofs are recorded above. Strict health passed including integrity/history_drift; existing advisory warnings remain. Initial test projection compile errors were corrected before the successful gates. No new PM CLI/SDK defects identified. Automatic result tracking remains disabled by existing policy; these sanitized comments retain evidence. Rebuild dist and regenerate/check changelog after final tracker writes. Release claim and retain in_progress for orchestrator verification."
